    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1250">

                <pb facs="0870" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/387.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following was telegraphed to Consul, Tampico, on August 4: [Quotes telegram of
                    August 4, 1914, to Vice Consul Bevan.]</p>
                <p>Consul has replied as follows: [Quotes telegram of August 6, 1914, from Vice
                    Consul Bevan.]</p>
                <p>Bring this matter most forcibly to General Carranza’s attention and urge that the
                    decrees providing for unjust levies of taxes at Tampico be withdrawn, as they
                    appear to be excessive and discriminatory and will result in closing down
                    industrial institutions and thus be injurious to the welfare of Mexico. Request
                    him to telegraph adequate order to Nafarrate,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
